KG42.register("rules-811ab76d4d9527f2d2705c77",{"id":"46-commercial_building_transactive_control::v141-c-R008","paper":"46-commercial_building_transactive_control","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R008","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Prosumer participation","process_stage":"participation","market_meaning":"Cooling sources may participate as sellers of chilled water in the central-HVAC water market. Scope: Thermal-energy supplier participation in the central-HVAC internal water market.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function participation.prosumer under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["participation.prosumer"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"Thermal-energy supplier participation in the central-HVAC internal water market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e02","v141-b-g01-e04"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Cooling sources may participate as sellers of chilled water in the central-HVAC water market. Scope: Thermal-energy supplier participation in the central-HVAC internal water market.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.prosumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e02","v141-b-g01-e04"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e02","location":{"location_id":"src-0abd014fd6-p02-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":", g pp y ve support real time price. Under the real time price, HVAC systems are s- merely price tak","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 1","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Two types of HVAC systems commonly serve commercial buildings: central systems and roof-top unit (RTU) systems. As illustrated in Fig. 1, a central system consists of a cooling source, a heating source, m (m ≥ 1) air handling units (AHUs), and n terminals (n ≥ m). The cooling (or heating) source generates cooling (or heating) energy that is then transferred to AHUs via hydraulic loops. AHUs can be categorized as multi- or single-zone, according to the number of zones the AHUs serve."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e04","location":{"location_id":"src-0abd014fd6-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"ventilation, and air conditioning system. et Table 3 ng Summary of markets in the transactive contro","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 3","table_id":"Table 3","image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Specifically, as illustrated in Fig. 3, the TC for the central systems consists of n air markets, one water market, and one electricity market. Table 3 summarizes the commodity, the buyers, and the sellers of each market. Note that a component of the TC can be a buyer and a seller simultaneously. For example, AHUs are the buyers in the water market and electricity market and the sellers in the air market, simultaneously.\nTable 3 Summary of markets in the transactive control for the central heating, ventilation, and air conditioning system.\nMarket | Commodity | Buyers | Sellers\nAir | Cooling air | Zones | AHUs\nWater | Chilled water | Air handling units (AHUs) | Cooling sources\nElectricity | Electricity | AHUs, cooling sources | Utility"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"The source support is a market-role/admission statement about cooling sources as sellers; it does not define a design selection or operational decision variable for this rule.","empty_theta_reason":"The rule contains no numeric, symbolic, or fixed input parameter for participation eligibility in the supplied source texts."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"participation.prosumer","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e04","quote":"Market | Commodity | Buyers | Sellers\nAir | Cooling air | Zones | AHUs\nWater | Chilled water | Air handling units (AHUs) | Cooling sources"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e02","quote":"The cooling (or heating) source generates cooling (or heating) energy that is then transferred to AHUs via hydraulic loops."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"58d30f307c22dc64c39d96e07edcbe56694324ad80db23c7c26a80b5ce3fff82","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen rule is a participation/admission statement: the source assigns cooling sources as sellers of chilled water in the central-HVAC water market and describes their physical role in supplying cooling energy to AHUs. No quantitative equation, optimization variable, design variable, or fixed parameter is defined for this participation scope. The B evidence remains unreviewed; this assessment relies only on the supplied source texts.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R008-C001","node_ids":["participation.prosumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The existing procedural constraint records the source-supported seller/participant role of cooling sources in the central-HVAC water market. The frozen graph has the participation.prosumer node and no edges for this unary role, so the binding is to that node only."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
